<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="MCP">
  <data key="d0">MCP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MCP, or Model Context Protocol, is an open-source protocol launched by Anthropic in November 2024. Its primary purpose is to standardize the integration of large language models (LLMs) with various external tools, resources, and prompts. The protocol defines how clients interact with servers to list and call these tools, resources, and prompts, typically via JSON-RPC 2.0 messages. This allows agents and workflows to natively connect and invoke tools and applications without the need for custom glue code.

MCP is designed to be a versatile and collaborative mechanism. It supports multi-model and multi-agent interactions within AI assistants and can be used to provide services and tools, such as chart generation, to language models. For instance, it works with systems like GPT-Vis to enable large models to produce visualizations from a single sentence. The protocol is also integral to platforms like Dify, where it serves as a service configuration that provides tools and resources to Agent nodes and allows resources and prompts to be used as tools. When connecting Dify to an MCPHub, MCP is one of the suggested connection methods, alongside SSE.

The implementation and deployment of MCP involve several practical considerations. It can be added locally and invoked through an MCPHub, with connection methods including SSE and MCP. It is also referenced in the context of deploying services like `antvis/mcp-server-chart`, which may require a remote service to function. A key challenge discussed is that having too many tools can cause complexity and exceed a model's context window. To address this, a proposed solution is to limit the number of MCP tools, for example, by implementing only one or two chart-generation tools so that models like Qwen3:32b can successfully invoke them. The protocol's underlying principles, its integration with large models, and troubleshooting model capability are also subjects of discussion. Furthermore, MCP is a concept that can be extended by building a local MCP platform or writing custom MCP services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf33c09cef21a9234b885adc19237c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6331e7987020e8aab4119b9099c8c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd9edaf2d6d316a2d66cb563a7b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36f33d14dcadc9d9f0360473719433d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f8c4393df9c460f378b7662edd6707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd96a7b68c52bd13466193e24646560d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e438aec0e2c5ce9de0dd0bb23713997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d9cd3023643e2df6531a006385352f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0825df065525dd92af8d2c20f70b3388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d350e3bb80f0fef24e7c96667c4d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8df96894d64e07a9d6fc07e19e8f283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68766f592d5fea97b491b07c0e727f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f8883c6fffe7e65586c4a3b4ad8f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af0cb0c15a552c37fc70116a7ff063ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb20a950ebc664cec0ec504d03fed297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c6000d6de041c5bcf23c16a5e559e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5e894e81be3f4f149dd2361ff4710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f6b87323bdb838bd0839433c2a27ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc458fff436dfae5dc91224ef0d7b0dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cb0f2f468eb972869d2a51b23a64211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215f43fa31733949908bb507a3fa6f2c</data>
