<node id="Dify">
  <data key="d0">Dify</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Dify is a low-code AI application development platform designed for building, testing, and deploying conversational AI workflows and agent-based applications. It features a visual workflow editor with nodes, configuration panels, and preview capabilities, enabling users to configure agent workflows, manage tool-call recursion depth, and test model tool-calling capabilities. Dify is widely used as a large model interaction framework, including in the Sanic-Web project and for the General Q&amp;A capability, and it supports testing small models' ability to invoke MCP services.

A central aspect of Dify is its integration with the Model Context Protocol (MCP). Starting from version v1.6.0, Dify supports two-way MCP, allowing users to call any MCP server or publish their own. Dify apps can be exposed as MCP servers for any client to invoke, and the platform can quickly integrate local MCP services. It is frequently referenced in the context of connecting to MCPHub and invoking MCP tools, though multiple accounts note that this connection is unstable, with usage depending on specific methods such as SSE or MCP and analyzable through logs. In some cases, users connected Dify to MCPHub but were unable to invoke MCP tools. Dify is also referenced in testing scenarios under the section path "Imagine if &gt; Dify测试," related to model tool calls and MCP service integration.

Dify additionally supports a plugin system, including offline plugin installation for multi-platform, multi-architecture, and cross-architecture deployments, making it suitable for pure intranet and restricted network environments. It provides configuration options for signature verification and allows installation of plugins not listed on the Dify Marketplace, which carries associated security risks. Overall, Dify serves as a versatile platform for AI workflow development, MCP service integration, and plugin management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf33c09cef21a9234b885adc19237c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab9af9f795cd884fa4b6080b8c4cbd2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6331e7987020e8aab4119b9099c8c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac52de499112f50a44504163e36d0194&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd9edaf2d6d316a2d66cb563a7b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-028b6088d3cdecf0364e7e5da0b83b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36f33d14dcadc9d9f0360473719433d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f8c4393df9c460f378b7662edd6707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52d758854de5931b6a611e1204d51bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d9cd3023643e2df6531a006385352f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6746154ee72afea8c47d8e88a7e50e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46e12b3f95e745beb9427a8d2c356fd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8df96894d64e07a9d6fc07e19e8f283&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796cca4fcff695d899b8a0523c299544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f8883c6fffe7e65586c4a3b4ad8f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d14809c97d977d90b6981933292df49d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af0cb0c15a552c37fc70116a7ff063ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c6000d6de041c5bcf23c16a5e559e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-981b9086710d6ccd0c9a98a302e00c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cfd720b0bb2ed54aa4a2374dc11cca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d94e514b546c10ac25541d2ef917278a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5ad16c20174c91752cb2d9fe2947a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4763d461b0f95b8e08fd85bc46bd41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4544b923b8a7b39d6d44d1fa30b59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e8a2ff85ae807c2af6a13dc42642923&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5e894e81be3f4f149dd2361ff4710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f6b87323bdb838bd0839433c2a27ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f28345b99168d6f816c3bff9402b4a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc458fff436dfae5dc91224ef0d7b0dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e3b316c15841047ae8db2e5bc076a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215f43fa31733949908bb507a3fa6f2c</data>
