</node>
<node id="Gpt-Vis-Api">
  <data key="d0">Gpt-Vis-Api</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gpt-Vis-Api is a chart generation API service that can be deployed locally or accessed as a cloud-based API. It is deployed by apconw (also referenced as the apconw/gpt-vis-api deployment) and is designed to receive JSON data requests, use AntV/G to generate various chart types—including line charts, bar charts, and organization charts—and then upload the resulting chart images to MinIO storage. After upload, the service returns pre-signed (presigned) URLs that allow frontend access to the generated images.

The service typically runs locally on port 3100, accepting POST requests at an endpoint such as http://localhost:3100/generate to produce charts and return URLs to the generated images. Its project files are located at E:\gpt-vis-api-main. Deployment involves local testing and Dify testing as part of its setup process. The service has also been described as a chart generation MCP service, and it has produced log output, for example on 2025-11-24 11:57:41, generating a JSON configuration for an organization chart.

In some usage scenarios, Gpt-Vis-Api is described as a cloud-based API that local models attempt to call, possibly represented by a cloud icon in related imagery. However, attempts by the Qwen3:32b model to call Gpt-Vis-Api successfully have failed, both in general and specifically within a Docker environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf33c09cef21a9234b885adc19237c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dfd9edaf2d6d316a2d66cb563a7b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-028b6088d3cdecf0364e7e5da0b83b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545b90e2cab5ad4d8fede3a9c2c4f58f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da2e3ba09aaf5c26f390a62fa29f730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9208d3d4d0af3445436567fdc54112d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0825df065525dd92af8d2c20f70b3388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5702ae24a0f62f9c64271f9c3ff84f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215f43fa31733949908bb507a3fa6f2c</data>
