<node id="SSE Log">
  <data key="d0">SSE Log</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The SSE log is a terminal screenshot capturing a communication session between a client and the MCP server, prefixed with session ID [SSE:c10e2988-ab9d-453c-8b59-d352158e943b], showing the sequence of JSON-RPC method calls and their results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MCP HTTP With SSE Client">
  <data key="d0">MCP HTTP With SSE Client</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MCP HTTP with SSE client is a Python HTTP client (python-httpx/0.27.2) version 1.0.0 that connects to the MCP server and sends JSON-RPC requests such as initialize, notifications/initialized, tools/list, resources/list, resources/templates/list, and prompts/list.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initialize Method">
  <data key="d0">Initialize Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The initialize method is a JSON-RPC 2.0 request with protocolVersion 2024-11-05 that succeeded, establishing the session between the client and the MCP server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tools/List Method">
  <data key="d0">Tools/List Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The tools/list method is a JSON-RPC request with id 1 that succeeded, returning the list of available tools from the MCP server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resources/List Method">
  <data key="d0">Resources/List Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The resources/list method is a JSON-RPC request with id 2 that failed with error code -32601 (Method not found).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615463</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resources/Templates/List Method">
  <data key="d0">Resources/Templates/List Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The resources/templates/list method is a JSON-RPC request with id 3 that failed with error code -32601 (Method not found).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prompts/List Method">
  <data key="d0">Prompts/List Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The prompts/list method is a JSON-RPC request with id 4 that failed with error code -32601 (Method not found), after which the log ends abruptly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chart Generation Tools">
  <data key="d0">Chart Generation Tools</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chart generation tools are one or two MCP tools that could be self-implemented to limit the number of MCP tools, potentially enabling Qwen3:32b to invoke them successfully.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notifications/Initialized Method">
  <data key="d0">Notifications/Initialized Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The notifications/initialized method is a JSON-RPC notification sent by the client after initialization, logged as 'RPC undefined notifications/initialized'.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Host.Docker.Internal:1122">
  <data key="d0">Host.Docker.Internal:1122</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Host.docker.internal:1122 is the network address where the MCP server is running and to which the client connects.&lt;SEP&gt;Host.docker.internal:1122 is the host header value in the request headers received by the MCP server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9f3e6cbaad85774625cbce27c7b8383</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSON-RPC 2.0">
  <data key="d0">JSON-RPC 2.0</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">JSON-RPC 2.0 is the message protocol used for communication between the client and the MCP server in the log.&lt;SEP&gt;JSON-RPC 2.0 is the remote procedure call protocol used for communication between the client and the MCP server, with requests carrying methods, ids, and params.&lt;SEP&gt;JSON-RPC 2.0 is the protocol used for requests and responses between the client and the MCP server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d350e3bb80f0fef24e7c96667c4d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cb0f2f468eb972869d2a51b23a64211</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protocol Version 2024-11-05">
  <data key="d0">Protocol Version 2024-11-05</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Protocol version 2024-11-05 is the protocolVersion specified in the initialize request params.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Error Code -32601">
  <data key="d0">Error Code -32601</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Error code -32601 with message 'Method not found' is returned by the MCP server for unsupported methods such as resources/list, resources/templates/list, and prompts/list.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RPC 5 Tools/Call">
  <data key="d0">RPC 5 Tools/Call</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">RPC 5 tools/call is the tool invocation call that Qwen3:32b failed to make, causing it to get stuck.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-629ff97ba9b08501fb91ecc6de8ffc80</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="孙青扬">
  <data key="d0">孙青扬</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">孙青扬is the author who responded to无趣's question, explaining that Dify connections are unstable and suggesting analyzing logs based on the specific connection method (SSE/MCP).&lt;SEP&gt;孙青扬is the author who provides guidance on connecting Dify to MCPHub and suggests analyzing logs to determine the specific connection method (SSE/MCP) due to instability.&lt;SEP&gt;孙青扬is identified as an author who responds to user comments in a discussion thread.&lt;SEP&gt;孙青扬is the author who responds to Amoypark's question, confirming that the described offline deployment approach is how it is done.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd96a7b68c52bd13466193e24646560d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d9cd3023643e2df6531a006385352f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46e12b3f95e745beb9427a8d2c356fd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc458fff436dfae5dc91224ef0d7b0dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
