<node id="MCP Service">
  <data key="d0">MCP Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MCP Service refers to a service based on the Model Context Protocol (MCP), a protocol-based interface that provides tools for large language models to invoke, typically through tools/call requests. It is designed to be integrated with models such as Qwen3:32b and DeepSeek:70b, and is used for tasks including chart and graph generation. In practice, MCP Service can be deployed in various forms: as a local service that Dify can quickly integrate with, as local services added to MCPHub that provide MCP tools, or as an ant-provided remote service, specifically mcp-server-chart, which requires a remote service to operate. One concrete implementation is started via the command "node build/index.js --transport sse" and runs on port 1122 for generating charts. MCP Service also involves configuration and deployment steps, including offline deployment scenarios where plugins are downloaded and packaged into image files for use on offline servers. However, there are noted limitations and challenges: DeepSeek 70b is unable to invoke it locally, and the service may be too complex with too many tools, potentially causing token overflow. The service has been the subject of technology selection discussions and is configured within agents to generate charts and graphs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e438aec0e2c5ce9de0dd0bb23713997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9f3e6cbaad85774625cbce27c7b8383&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52d758854de5931b6a611e1204d51bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da2e3ba09aaf5c26f390a62fa29f730&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d8028699a132034eca5b3a45821eee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46e12b3f95e745beb9427a8d2c356fd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22289987ab43c6909c9d91c1d8530ece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796cca4fcff695d899b8a0523c299544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb20a950ebc664cec0ec504d03fed297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b546446cf6afd391433a0d3a55406647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5702ae24a0f62f9c64271f9c3ff84f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f4544b923b8a7b39d6d44d1fa30b59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc458fff436dfae5dc91224ef0d7b0dc</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tool Call Failure">
  <data key="d0">Tool Call Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tool Call Failure refers to the problem where a model returns tool calls without producing results, as described in the surrounding text.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool call failure is an issue where the backend monitoring showed the large model successfully accessed port 1122 and transmitted data, but the tool invocation was reported as failed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fda34b6704d5dded4db6263706653770&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cfd720b0bb2ed54aa4a2374dc11cca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User">
  <data key="d0">User</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The User is a person interacting with the Dify chat interface, asking about military facilities in Taitung County and requesting a combined text and chart answer.&lt;SEP&gt;The user is an individual who shared feedback and reported that their model, Llama3.3, only returns tool calls without returning results.&lt;SEP&gt;The User is an individual who uses Llama3.3 and experiences issues where the model keeps returning tool calls instead of results.&lt;SEP&gt;The User is represented by a robot icon and interacts with the AI Model by asking questions and receiving final results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fda34b6704d5dded4db6263706653770&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52d758854de5931b6a611e1204d51bb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-981b9086710d6ccd0c9a98a302e00c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cfd720b0bb2ed54aa4a2374dc11cca</data>
