</node>
<node id="MCP Tool">
  <data key="d0">MCP Tool</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MCP tools are functionalities provided by MCP servers that can be invoked by clients such as Dify through MCPHub.&lt;SEP&gt;MCP Tool refers to the tools provided by MCP services that could not be invoked when Dify was connected to MCPHub.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c6746154ee72afea8c47d8e88a7e50e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc458fff436dfae5dc91224ef0d7b0dc</data>
