</node>
<node id="Mcptest.Py">
  <data key="d0">Mcptest.Py</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Mcptest.Py is a FastMCP service test script that lists available tools (weather, stock) and demonstrates weather queries, stock queries, and error handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Mcptest.py is a Python file located in the HGMCP folder alongside mcpserver.py in the VS Code Explorer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-677387b0d12710d9b55ebc13fd550e1e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sql生成Test Mcp">
  <data key="d0">Sql生成Test Mcp</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Sql生成Test Mcp is a Dify workflow that connects to an MCP server and uses a ReAct agent with the qwen3:8b model to perform weather and stock queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ReAct Agent">
  <data key="d0">ReAct Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The ReAct agent is an agent strategy in Dify that supports MCP tools, configured with the qwen3:8b model and a maximum of 5 iterations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qwen3:8b">
  <data key="d0">Qwen3:8b</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Qwen3:8b is the chat model used by the ReAct agent in the Dify workflow.&lt;SEP&gt;Qwen3:8b is a model mentioned in the caption as being able to call the simple MCP service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-677387b0d12710d9b55ebc13fd550e1e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mcp Server Configuration">
  <data key="d0">Mcp Server Configuration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The MCP server configuration is a JSON setting in Dify specifying the transport as 'sse' and the URL as 'http://host.docker.internal:4200/demo'.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Localhost:4200">
  <data key="d0">Localhost:4200</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Localhost:4200 is the local address and port where the FastMCP HTTP service runs with the path '/demo'.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mcp">
  <data key="d0">Mcp</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MCP (Model Context Protocol) is a protocol used to connect external tool servers to AI agent workflows, as demonstrated by the Dify agent connecting to a local MCP server.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Start Node">
  <data key="d0">Start Node</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Start node is the initial node in the Dify workflow that provides the user query input to the Agent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Reply Node">
  <data key="d0">Direct Reply Node</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Direct Reply node is the final node in the Dify workflow that outputs the Agent's text response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-886c2e8ce4df58fde41127defb87413b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/RAG-Anything-reproduction/data/MCP服务.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791615476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
